cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "codonamr: codon usage analysis of antimicrobial resistance genes, with validated controls"
abstract: >-
  codonamr takes sequence identifiers, fetches the coding sequences, resolves
  the source organism to a RefSeq reference genome, computes the standard
  codon-usage indices, and applies a length-matched null and a per-nucleotide
  composition control. The controls are validated by injecting an association
  of known size and by injecting none.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Victor"
    given-names: "Manish Prakash"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-22
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/bioforkgithub/codonamr"
keywords:
  - codon usage
  - antimicrobial resistance
  - codon adaptation index
  - effective number of codons
  - bioinformatics
